# Free-standing graphene monolayer (OER tutorial fixture): 2 C atoms,
# primitive hexagonal cell (a = 2.46 Ang), 20 Ang vacuum along c, split
# evenly on both sides (frac z = 0.5) -- the SAME fixture 4.13-her's own
# example uses (deliberate: it keeps the whole HER/OER example pair
# directly comparable, and free-standing rather than one-sided lets this
# one structure also exercise stb-oer's own --both-sides flag). Small and
# fast on purpose: every real SIESTA relaxation/single-point step in this
# walkthrough is FABRICATED (see the README's worked-example section), so
# this structure only ever needs to be big enough to exercise
# stb-oer/stb-oerIntermediates/stb-oerRefs' own file-writing mechanics,
# never actually relaxed for real. Graphene itself is chemically a POOR
# OER catalyst (no transition-metal center to stabilize the OH*/O*/OOH*
# sequence the way an oxide does) -- fitting for a methodology
# demonstration, not a material you'd actually screen for real.
SystemName graphene monolayer (OER tutorial fixture)
SystemLabel siesta

LatticeConstant 1.0 Ang
%block LatticeVectors
  2.4600000000   0.0000000000   0.0000000000
 -1.2300000000   2.1304224390   0.0000000000
  0.0000000000   0.0000000000  20.0000000000
%endblock LatticeVectors

NumberOfSpecies 1
%block ChemicalSpeciesLabel
 1   6   C
%endblock ChemicalSpeciesLabel

NumberOfAtoms 2
AtomicCoordinatesFormat Fractional
%block AtomicCoordinatesAndAtomicSpecies
 0.000000000   0.000000000   0.500000000   1
 0.333333333   0.666666667   0.500000000   1
%endblock AtomicCoordinatesAndAtomicSpecies
